  "lineage": "Filipino harana (\"serenade\") nineteenth-and-twentieth-century romantic-courtship vocal tradition of the Tagalog and broader lowland-Christian Philippine communities, in which young men serenaded young women at their windows accompanied by acoustic guitar. The form derives from Spanish-colonial seventeenth-eighteenth century romance song-tradition adapted with Tagalog-Visayan language and Philippine-tropical sensibility. Performance: small-group of male singers (often with the principal suitor) with acoustic-guitar accompaniment, performing standard repertoire of harana-classics or improvising. The form survived as a vestigial-cultural practice through the twentieth century and entered post-2000s urban-revival contexts through documentary projects and folk-music ensembles.",
